USB CDC ACM: a full TX buffer is flushed by poll_out() and fifo_fill().

6d69698de74 ("cdc_acm: tx throughput improvements", merged 2026-09-25)
replaced the TX ring buffer with net_bufs. Data is written into one `current`
64 B buffer, and handing a full one to the USB stack is left to tx_fifo_work.
Two callers cannot wait for that work item.

poll_out(): a printk burst from a thread that does not yield (a packet log
line is 100-300 B) fills the buffer and every further byte is discarded ("No
TX buffer available, discard data") because the work item cannot run
meanwhile: RAW hex cut after ~64 B, RX lines losing their start, CLI replies
such as `get public.key` corrupted. The old ring buffer accepted ~1 KB per
burst. Enqueue the full buffer from poll_out() (thread context only) and retry
once. It never blocks, so an unplugged host cannot hang the caller; bytes are
dropped only when the buffer pool is exhausted, as before the rewrite.

fifo_fill(): it enqueues a buffer only after writing into it. When `current`
is already full on entry it accepts 0 bytes, while irq_tx_ready() reports
space (cdc_acm_tx_fifo_space_get() counts the free pool buffers once the echo
mitigation is done). A UART ISR that loops while the driver reports a pending
interrupt, as the Zephyr samples and ZephyrCompanionUSB.cpp do, then never
returns; it runs on the work queue that would run tx_fifo_work, so nothing
flushes the buffer and every thread below the work queue starves. `current`
is full on entry when poll_out() filled it (boot log, banner) or when it was
filled before the echo mitigation, whose flush is scheduled
CONFIG_USBD_CDC_ACM_TX_DELAY_MS (100 ms) after the host opens the port: a
reply sent in that window hangs the node. Enqueue the full buffer from
fifo_fill() and retry once.

Suspended bus (host asleep with the port open): cdc_acm_tx_fifo_enqueue() does
nothing while CDC_ACM_CLASS_SUSPENDED is set, so the free pool buffers are not
usable either and the same loop spins on the next frame. Report only the
current buffer's tailroom while suspended. Queued data goes out with the next
TX enable or RX after the resume. From the code; not reproduced on hardware.

poll_out(): found 2026-09-26 with a rak3401_1watt repeater +
packet_logging.conf feeding mctomqtt. fifo_fill(): found 2026-10-03 on a
wio_tracker_l1 debug companion (silent on USB whenever the first host action
after boot was a CLI frame, BLE still advertising). Neither is fixed on Zephyr
main as of ac03a4a9085; no upstream issue found.

